  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHD: Prevention, mediation and resolution of political conflicts in Tunisia (2014)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The HD Centre facilitates discussions between key political actors to tackle potentially conflict inducing issues in a protected, non-public space. When tensions are too high to convene rounds of dialogue, the HD Centre conducts mediation and shuttle diplomacy. The space provided by the HD Centre allows Tunisian political actors to formulate compromise solutions to political problems and encourages more consensual forms of decision-making. This reduces political tensions and allows conflicts to be resolved or prevented.
Project activities will be focused on the following areas:
1. High-level Crisis mediation/ dialogue: 
2. Dialogue on Elections 
3. Dialogue on Political Polarisation and Women&#xbf;s Rights</narrative>
  </description>
